  "body": "The work of #1649 carries a flipped WCS X or Y through the post. Only the scripts that declare `axisInversion = true` (`fanuc.cps`, `haas.cps`) post a flipped WCS. Each other mill script refuses a flipped WCS by name: mazak, doosan-dnm, sinumerik, heidenhain, mach4, grblhal, tormach, tinyg and carvera.\n\nThe maintainer's words (2026-11-17), quoted in #1649: \"the ability to flip axis from a positive to negative is fundamental and should not be blocked.. posting and generation should take it into consideration rather..\"\n\nA user with one of these posts cannot post a flipped WCS. The workaround is to clear the flip or to choose Fanuc or Haas.\n\nFor each script:\n- Run the mirrored stream of `crates/post/tests/wcs_flip.rs` through it and trace the program with a controller reader that has the flipped axis.\n- Check the dialect's own words that a mirror changes: arc centres (incremental or absolute, for example Heidenhain CC), the compensation words (RL/RR on Heidenhain), helical arcs, cycles and probing.\n- When the trace is on the CAM path, declare `axisInversion = true` in the script and add the script to the test's case list.\n\nThis also carries the #374 machine axis inversion to the same scripts, because the two use the same flag.\n\nDone means: each mill script either declares `axisInversion = true` with a passing equivalence test, or has a recorded reason why it cannot.\n",
